From 28fb0162ece4b6c734eed706300368fd6bb9c4aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 08:38:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(corun): CC 71-78 per-frame detent coalesce for
 move_native (PR-94 item 6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per the maintainer review:

> CC 71–78 coalescing has to ship with move_native, not as follow-up.
> The knob stutter you documented will get filed as a Schwung bug the
> first week it's in users' hands. Per-frame detent collapse in the
> shim before forwarding to Move firmware.

Implemented in the pre-ioctl filter loop in schwung_shim.c: when the
tool cedes CORUN_GRP_KNOBS to Move firmware (the default), incoming
CC 71-78 detents are summed into a per-knob accumulator within the
audio frame; the individual events are suppressed (filter=1), and at
the end of the loop one consolidated CC per knob is injected into the
first empty sh_midi slot. Cumulative deltas are clamped to the one-byte
signed encoding (±63); anything beyond that spills to the next frame
naturally on the next inbound detent.

Move firmware's per-CC cost (~900µs for synth-param write + OLED redraw)
times multiple back-to-back detents in a single audio frame is what
overran the SPI window. Capping at one CC per frame keeps the spike
budget bounded while preserving the cumulative knob travel.

The coalesce is gated on CORUN_TARGET_MOVE_NATIVE + CORUN_GRP_KNOBS NOT
in keep_mask, so tools that route the knobs themselves are unaffected.
---
 src/schwung_shim.c | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 52 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/schwung_shim.c b/src/schwung_shim.c
