MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

One-page co-run reference: the two targets and what each cedes by
default, the framework exit gesture (Back) plus the CORUN_KEEP_BACK
opt-out for tools that need Back free for peer navigation, the JS API
(shadow_corun_begin / shadow_corun_end / shadow_corun_state) with the
CORUN_TARGET_* / CORUN_GRP_* / CORUN_KEEP_DEFAULT / CORUN_KEEP_BACK
globals, the capability gate pattern for tools shipping against both
stock and patched Schwung, the Move-firmware coupling caveat that
motivates the CC 71-78 per-frame coalesce, and one note on the single
source of truth — corun_event_owner() — so any future contributor can
add a target by extending one helper rather than hunting mirror checks.

PR-94 item 7.
---
