Refines the CORUN_KEEP_BACK opt-out for CORUN_TARGET_CHAIN_EDIT
specifically. The chain editor lives inside shadow_ui (same process
as the framework dispatch) and owns its own view stack, so shadow_ui
can tell when the editor is at its top-level CHAIN_EDIT view vs.
deeper inside (component edit, patches, hierarchy, etc.).

shadow_ui's Back handler now:
- in sub-views: handleBack() to pop one level
- at CHAIN_EDIT (top): calls shadow_corun_end() itself

This gives the chain-edit target the original "Back exits at top,
navigates within" UX you described in review, even though the tool
opted out of the framework's broader Back-reservation. Move-native
keeps the opt-out semantic (Back goes to Move firmware, tool exits
via its own gesture) because Move's UI depth isn't observable from
the framework side.

No tool-side changes required — dAVEBOx's pollDSP picks up
target=NONE on the next frame and runs its existing exit cleanup
when shadow_ui ends the session.
