Subject: [PATCH] feat(corun): uniform coRunWants() for all UI-element
 intercept guards
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Generalize the co-run intercept so which control groups an overlay/editor owns is
driven solely by the tool's keep_mask, with no per-element special-casing.
coRunWants(grp) now = (overlay ? KEEPS : CEDES) — the keep-based predicate is the
overlay analogue of chain-edit's cede-based one. Apply it to every guard (jog,
back, knobs, shift, track, knob-touch), and generalize the knob-touch note gate
to coRunUiActive(). A tool enables FX-knob editing in an overlay just by keeping
CORUN_GRP_KNOBS (+ TOUCH for the param pop-up). Chain-edit unchanged (corunOverlayId
null → coRunWants == coRunCedes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
